            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `saw\"` turns `word` into `\"word \"` I don't know why I am getting that extra space at the end and would like not to :) I am just using a black setup for mini.surround.\r\n\r\nHere is a breakdown of `saw\"`:\r\n- `sa` initiates adding surrounding. Waits for user to input any kind of motion/textobject (on which surrounding will be added).\r\n- `w` serves as that motion/textobject. It is a word motion (see `:h w`) which moves cursor at the start of next word. Which means that surrounding will be added at the region between current cursor position (included) and up until start of next word (excluded). This means including whitespace after current word.\r\n- `\"` indicates which surrounding you want to add (pair `\"` in this case).\r\n\r\nSo to not include whitespace after current word use `iw` textobject (see `:h iw`). In this case it would be `saiw\"`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">saw\"</code> turns <code class=\"notranslate\">word</code> into <code class=\"notranslate\">\"word \"</code> I don't know why I am getting that extra space at the end and would like not to :) I am just using a black setup for mini.surround.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is a breakdown of <code class=\"notranslate\">saw\"</code>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code> initiates adding surrounding. Waits for user to input any kind of motion/textobject (on which surrounding will be added).</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">w</code> serves as that motion/textobject. It is a word motion (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h w</code>) which moves cursor at the start of next word. Which means that surrounding will be added at the region between current cursor position (included) and up until start of next word (excluded). This means including whitespace after current word.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> indicates which surrounding you want to add (pair <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> in this case).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So to not include whitespace after current word use <code class=\"notranslate\">iw</code> textobject (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h iw</code>). In this case it would be <code class=\"notranslate\">saiw\"</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "saw\" turns word into \"word \" I don't know why I am getting that extra space at the end and would like not to :) I am just using a black setup for mini.surround.\n\nHere is a breakdown of saw\":\n\nsa initiates adding surrounding. Waits for user to input any kind of motion/textobject (on which surrounding will be added).\nw serves as that motion/textobject. It is a word motion (see :h w) which moves cursor at the start of next word. Which means that surrounding will be added at the region between current cursor position (included) and up until start of next word (excluded). This means including whitespace after current word.\n\" indicates which surrounding you want to add (pair \" in this case).\n\nSo to not include whitespace after current word use iw textobject (see :h iw). In this case it would be saiw\".",
